## 1. Executive Summary

This document presents the Carbon Footprint Analysis for MedSync Health for the fiscal year 2024 (FY 2024), establishing a baseline for the company's environmental impact in alignment with our commitment to corporate social responsibility (CSR) and the goals outlined in **OPS-010: Sustainability Policy**. The total calculated carbon equivalent emissions for FY 2024 were **2,850 tonnes of CO₂e (tCO₂e)**.

The analysis follows the Greenhouse Gas (GHG) Protocol, categorizing emissions into three scopes. As a global healthcare technology company with 1,200 employees [1] and a primary focus on cloud-based services, the majority of our emissions fall under Scope 3 (Value Chain), specifically from purchased cloud computing services and employee-related activities.

| Scope | Description | FY 2024 Emissions (tCO₂e) | Percentage of Total |
|:---|:---|:---:|:---:|
| **Scope 1** | Direct Emissions (Owned/Controlled Sources) | 15 | 0.5% |
| **Scope 2** | Indirect Emissions (Purchased Energy) | 835 | 29.3% |
| **Scope 3** | Other Indirect Emissions (Value Chain) | 2,000 | 70.2% |
| **Total** | | **2,850** | **100.0%** |

