## 3. Scope 2: Energy Indirect Emissions

Scope 2 emissions are generated from the consumption of purchased electricity for heating, cooling, and powering our office spaces. Emissions are calculated using the location-based method, reflecting the carbon intensity of the local electricity grids.

### 3.1. Office Footprint and Energy Consumption

MedSync Health operates four primary offices supporting a total headcount of 1,200 employees [1]. The total estimated office space is 140,000 sq ft.

| Office Location | Headcount [1] | Estimated Area (sq ft) | Annual Electricity (MWh) | Grid Emission Factor (tCO₂e/MWh) | FY 2024 Emissions (tCO₂e) |
|:---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|
| **Boston, MA (HQ)** | 650 | 65,000 | 975 | 0.35 | 341.25 |
| **London, UK** | 280 | 40,000 | 600 | 0.20 | 120.00 |
| **Berlin, Germany** | 150 | 20,000 | 300 | 0.45 | 135.00 |
| **Singapore** | 120 | 15,000 | 225 | 0.44 | 99.00 |
| **Total** | **1,200** | **140,000** | **2,100** | | **695.25** |

*Note: The remaining 139.75 tCO₂e in Scope 2 is attributed to district heating/cooling and other minor purchased utilities, bringing the total to 835 tCO₂e.*

### 3.2. Scope 2 Mitigation Strategy

In alignment with our sustainability goals, the Operations team will investigate Power Purchase Agreements (PPAs) for renewable energy in the Boston and London offices, which account for the largest share of our Scope 2 emissions. This initiative is detailed further in **STRAT-005: Global Real Estate Strategy**.

